FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://api.example.com

# Ticketing API

Stress example for the less common grammar corners: an enum data structure,
optional fields, action-level path overrides (a search action and a close
action living on other paths), resource-level plus action-level parameters,
and multiple alternative responses per action.

## Tickets Collection [/tickets]

+ Parameters
    + status (string, optional) - Filter the collection by ticket status.

### List tickets [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (array[Ticket])

### Search tickets [GET /tickets/search]

+ Parameters
    + q (string, required) - Full-text query string.
    + limit (number, optional) - Maximum number of results to return.

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (array[Ticket])

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Error)

## Ticket [/tickets/{id}]

+ Parameters
    + id (string, required) - Ticket identifier.

### Get a ticket [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Ticket)

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Error)

### Close a ticket [POST /tickets/{id}/close]

+ Request (application/json)
    + Attributes (CloseRequest)

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Ticket)

+ Response 409 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Error)

# Data Structures

## Ticket (object)
+ id: `T-100` (string, required) - Ticket identifier.
+ subject: `Printer on fire` (string, required) - Short subject line.
+ status: `open` (TicketStatus, required) - Lifecycle state.
+ assignee: `kai` (string, optional) - Current assignee, if any.
+ priority: 2 (number, optional) - Priority from 1 (highest) to 5.

## TicketStatus (enum)
+ open
+ pending
+ closed

## CloseRequest (object)
+ reason: `resolved` (string, required) - Why the ticket is being closed.

## Error (object)
+ code: `not_found` (string, required) - Machine-readable error code.
+ message: `Ticket not found` (string, required) - Human-readable message.
